## (4) Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale / trade-off |
|---|---|
| **Zero production dependencies** | Security/supply-chain simplicity, stable install size; forces hand-rolled color detection, spawn handling, Levenshtein. Policy documented in CONTRIBUTING. |
| **CommonJS core + thin ESM wrapper** (`esm.mjs`) | Avoids dual-package hazard; single source of truth with named ESM exports; slight indirection cost. |
| **EventEmitter as the option-value dispatch bus** | Decouples tokenizer from value semantics; but makes flow stringly-typed and harder to trace/refactor. |
| **Single-file `Command` monolith** | Historical accretion; enables cross-cutting state (parent/child, saved state) without module boundaries; high cognitive load and merge-friction. |
| **Value-source tracking** (`default/env/cli/implied/config`) | Enables precedence rules (env never overrides CLI; implied never overrides explicit) and `getOptionValueSource`. |
| **Class + factory-method extension model** | `createCommand/createOption/createArgument/createHelp` overridable — the primary supported customization seam (e.g., custom-command-class example). |
| **Structured errors + `exitOverride` instead of unconditional exits** | Makes the library embeddable/testable; default behavior still `process.exit` (CLI-first philosophy). |
| **Fail-noisily at declaration** | Duplicate flags/commands, malformed flags, mixed `-abc` short flags throw at registration, not at parse — catches author errors early. |
| **Breaking changes gated to majors, documented with migration tips** | Release-policy doc: ~6-month majors tied to Node LTS EOL; 12-month security window for older lines. |
| **Hand-written `.d.ts` + tsd, JSDoc checked by tsc** | Two validated type surfaces instead of generated types; drift risk accepted in exchange for control. |
| **`opts()` returns a plain object; legacy `storeOptionsAsProperties` retained** | Modern ergonomics + backward compatibility, but the legacy mode forbids repeated `parse()` (v13 breaking behavior). |
| **Negative numbers as option/command arguments (14.0.0)** | Regex heuristic (`/^-(\d+|\d*\.\d+)(e[+-]?\d+)?$/`) with a hierarchy check for digit short-flags — pragmatic, edge-case-prone. |
| **Modernization refactors in 14.0.1** | Optional chaining, object spread, in-place `parseOptions` arg processing, `_collectValue` push — readability/perf with subtle behavior risk in the hottest path. |
| **Help is WYSIWYG with side-effect tolerance** | `visibleArguments` mutates argument descriptions from legacy `_argsDescription`; historical behavior kept deliberately. |

