## (5) Risk Map

| # | Risk | Severity | Mitigation present | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| R1 | **Command monolith (87 KB / 2777 lines)** — regression blast radius and review load concentrated in one file | High | Extensive per-feature test files | Refactor into cohesive modules would itself be high-risk churn for a widely depended-upon library |
| R2 | **Stringly-typed event bus** (`option:<name>`) — collisions, typos, hard-to-follow flow; user could even register listeners on the same names | Medium | Name derived from canonical `Option.name()`; conflict checks at registration | Deep refactor risk; current design is load-bearing |
| R3 | **`process.exit()` inside library** (parse errors, help, executable close) | Medium-High | `exitOverride`; `_exitCallback` path | Any missed path silently kills embedding apps; spawn 'close' handler exits with code `?? 1` |
| R4 | **Hand-written typings drift** — runtime and `.d.ts` are separate sources of truth | Medium | `tsd` + `check:type:js` gates in CI | New features must land in 4 places (runtime, JSDoc, typings, test-d) |
| R5 | **Long-lived legacy APIs** (`storeOptionsAsProperties`, `InvalidOptionArgumentError`, regex `parseArg`, `addHelpCommand`, `noHelp`, `_argsDescription`, `command:*` events) | Medium | `docs/deprecated.md`, `deprecated.test.js` | Each constrains future parsing changes (e.g., multi-parse ban) |
| R6 | **Tokenizer edge cases** — negative-number heuristic, `--no-` interplay, `--` literal, variadic-option vs unknown-option ambiguity, pass-through modes | High | Large dedicated test files (parseOptions, positionalOptions, pass-through) | Any new flag syntax interacts with all modes |
| R7 | **Executable subcommand platform variance** — Windows spawn via `execPath`, extension search, symlink realpath, inspector-port increment, signal forwarding | Medium | Mock-based + real-spawn tests, 3-OS CI | `incrementNodeInspectorPort` is a heuristic that can misfire |
| R8 | **Help subsystem complexity** — 41 methods, side-effecting visibility, color conventions implemented by hand (NO_COLOR/FORCE_COLOR/CLICOLOR) | Medium | `help.*` test files, snapshots | Ecosystem color conventions evolve independently |
| R9 | **Node ≥ 20 floor tied to release cadence** — majors align with Node LTS EOL | Low-Medium | Release-policy doc now makes it predictable | Users on older Node pinned to older majors |
| R10 | **Test-suite global mutation** — tests rewrite `process.argv`, `process.versions.electron`, `process.defaultApp`, spawn mocks | Medium | Save/restore discipline per test | Isolation fragility; a leaked mutation causes cascading failures |
| R11 | **Dependency-update churn** (recent commits are mostly Dependabot bumps; eslint major, prettier) | Low | `npm run check` gates (lint/format/type) | Formatting/lint upgrades touch every file in `check:format` |

